      "argv": [
        "node",
        "/Users/brad/.cache/swarm-comparison/tools/swarm/dist/cli.js",
        "With the YAML 1.1 schema (YAML11_SCHEMA), timestamps whose year is between 0000 and 0099 are not recognized: load(\"- 0001-01-01\\n- 0050-06-15T12:30:00Z\", { schema: YAML11_SCHEMA }) returns plain strings instead of Date objects, and a Date in that range does not survive dump followed by load. Make such date-only and full timestamps resolve to Date values whose UTC year is the literal four-digit year written in the document (year 1, year 50), with calendar validation still rejecting dates that Date would normalize such as 0001-02-29 (which must stay a string, and must raise \"cannot resolve\" when tagged !!timestamp explicitly). Behavior for years 0100 and later must not change. Source is under src/ (TypeScript); the package is built with npm run build and tests run with node --test \"test/core/**/*.test.mjs\" \"test/spec/*.test.mjs\".\n\nVisible acceptance check (it must pass; it is not the only criterion): npm run build && node acceptance/visible/check.mjs\nThe project's own tests run with: node --test test/core/**/*.test.mjs test/spec/*.test.mjs\nDo not modify anything under acceptance/visible/.",
